 en:{beginnerPass:'A completed pass means the receiver got the ball. It does not, by itself, mean a chance was created.',beginnerInterception:'An interception stops a pass before its intended receiver gets it. Possession changes at this recorded touch.',beginnerRecovery:'A recovery means winning the ball back. Watch where the first pass goes next.',beginnerShot:'A shot is an attempt toward goal. The recorded result is {result}; speed alone cannot tell you the result.',mathPath:'Recorded straight-line ball path: {distance} m. This is not the route a player ran.',mathForward:'This completed pass moved the ball {distance} m toward the opponent’s goal, measured along the pitch.',mathBackward:'This completed pass moved the ball {distance} m toward the passer’s own goal. Negative net movement is not a failed calculation.',mathFlat:'This completed pass had no measured movement toward either goal along the pitch.',mathInterception:'Recorded ball path before the interception: {distance} m. It does not count as a completed pass.',mathRecovery:'This recovery changes possession; there is no completed-pass gain to assign to it.',mathShot:'Average speed over the recorded ball path: {speed} km/h. This is not peak speed or a scoring probability.',tacticalForward:'The completed pass advances the ball. Its record alone does not show whether a defensive line was broken.',tacticalBackward:'The completed pass moves toward the team’s own goal. It may reset the attack; the record does not establish why.',tacticalFlat:'The pass retains possession without measured forward progress. The next action will show whether play advances.',tacticalTurnover:'The recorded interception changes possession. Pressure may have preceded it, but this event alone does not prove what caused the error.',tacticalRecovery:'Possession is recovered. The next completed outlet is needed to describe the transition.',tacticalShot:'The move reaches a shot with a recorded result. The event does not establish the attacker’s intent or chance quality.',signedGain:'Net goal-directed movement on completed passes',negativeGain:'A negative value means the completed passes moved toward that team’s own goal overall.',positiveGain:'A positive value means movement toward the opponents’ goal overall.',zeroGain:'No net movement along the goal direction is recorded.',noPassGain:'No completed pass is available for a directional calculation.'},
